You are working in the DeepSeek Harness repository, which houses "Daliesk", an AI enterprise: a roster of 147 seats in 10 divisions (data/enterprise/roster.json), a ticket queue (data/enterprise/tickets/), a shift engine that ships tickets through reviewed programs (`pnpm run enterprise -- shift`), the ticketless divisions' functions (`pnpm run enterprise:functions`), a self-refilling intake (`pnpm run enterprise:intake`), all recorded in data/enterprise/ledger.jsonl, and a public command deck (apps/command-deck, GitHub Pages https://lbjlincoln.github.io/deepseek-harness/, data from `pnpm run enterprise:publish`). scripts/enterprise-scheduler.sh runs scripts/enterprise-cycle.sh every two hours unattended in a dedicated worktree: intake → shift → functions → roster → publish → push. Each cycle logs only to a container-local file, which the repository never sees and which a container reset erases, as happened at 22:07Z today. At 2026-09-29T15:00Z the operator must be given an honest, reproducible account of what the enterprise did in its first 24 hours unattended. You build that evidence: (1) a durable record of every cycle, (2) a deterministic report over any time window, (3) the deck's "last 24 hours" view.

Read first: CLAUDE.md, docs/testing.md, data/enterprise/README.md, scripts/enterprise-cycle.sh, scripts/enterprise-scheduler.sh, scripts/enterprise-ledger.ts, scripts/enterprise-publish.ts and its spec, scripts/enterprise-functions.ts (how it reads the GitHub REST API unauthenticated under NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 and maps Branch CI jobs), scripts/enterprise-roster.ts, apps/command-deck/README.md and apps/command-deck/components/enterprise/LedgerPanel.tsx, .agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-28-enterprise-functions-and-occupancy.md.

